<title>FRANCE: SGS-Thomson H1 net income falls.</title>
<headline>SGS-Thomson H1 net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable income		  182.6  vs	   351.1</p>
<p>    Net					    181.1  vs	   350.6</p>
<p>    Net attributable per share ($)	  1.31  vs	    2.53</p>
<p>    Operating				    229.4  vs	   445.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax					228.0  vs	   450.3</p>
<p>    Turnover				   1,914.6  vs	 2,075.0</p>
<p>    Gross margin				 735.0  vs	   906.5</p>
<p>Second quarter</p>
<p>    Net attributable income		   92.1  vs	   176.1</p>
<p>    Net					     91.8  vs	   175.8</p>
<p>    Net attributable per share ($)	  0.66  vs	     1.27</p>
<p>    Operating				    115.9  vs	   224.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax					115.2  vs	   222.7</p>
<p>    Turnover				     969.7  vs	 1,047.4</p>
<p>    Gross margin				 373.8  vs	   465.3</p>
<p>NOTE - SGS-Thomson Microelectronics NV said in a statement it saw a Q3 gross margin at the same level as Q2 and an improvement in Q4. It added it expected sales to rise in Q3 with an acceleration in Q4.</p>
</text>
